[{"id":"fm-core1-1.27-q1","number":1,"question":"<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.27/questions/assets/diagrams/127-q1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Identify each of the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> points on the polar coordinate grid above as polar coordinates, giving your answers in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(r,\\theta)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\pi&lt;\\theta\\le\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>State the point furthest from the pole <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>State the point closest to the pole <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nA(2,\\tfrac\\pi6)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nB(4,\\tfrac{5\\pi}{12})\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nC(8,\\tfrac{3\\pi}4)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nD(3,-\\tfrac{2\\pi}3)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nE(5,-\\tfrac\\pi2)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nF(\\tfrac52,-\\tfrac\\pi6)\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.27-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>Given each of the following points are polar coordinates, plot each on the same grid:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(2,\\frac\\pi2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B(5,\\frac{4\\pi}3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C(3,\\frac\\pi3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D(2,-\\frac\\pi3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"E(4,-\\frac{7\\pi}6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/127-p1-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.27-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>The following points are given as Cartesian coordinates. Find the polar form of each of the points giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(r,\\theta)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are both exact:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(5,-5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,2\\sqrt3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,-\\sqrt3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-3,\\sqrt3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/127-p2-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\theta=\\arctan(\\tfrac33)=\\frac\\pi4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr=\\sqrt{3^2+3^2}=\\sqrt{18}=3\\sqrt2\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3\\sqrt2,\\frac\\pi4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/127-p2-2.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\theta=\\arctan(\\tfrac55)=\\frac\\pi4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr=\\sqrt{5^2+5^2}=\\sqrt{50}=5\\sqrt2\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(5\\sqrt2,-\\frac\\pi4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/127-p3-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\theta=\\arctan(\\tfrac{2\\sqrt3}2)=\\frac\\pi3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr=\\sqrt{2^2+(2\\sqrt3)^2}=\\sqrt{16}=4\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,\\frac\\pi3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/127-p3-2.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\theta=\\arctan(\\sqrt3)=\\frac\\pi3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr=\\sqrt{1^2+(\\sqrt3)^2}=\\sqrt4=2\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,-\\frac{2\\pi}3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/127-p4-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\theta=\\arctan(\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}3)=\\frac\\pi6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr=\\sqrt{3^2+(\\sqrt3)^2}=\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt3\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2\\sqrt3,\\frac{5\\pi}6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.27-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>Find the principal polar coordinate of each of the following points given in Cartesian form giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(r,\\theta)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is exact and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is given to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> significant figures:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-2,5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-7,-24)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(12,-13)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/127-p4-2.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\theta=\\arctan(\\tfrac31)=1.25\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr=\\sqrt{1^2+3^2}=\\sqrt{10}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\sqrt{10},1.25)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/127-p5-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\theta=\\arctan(\\tfrac52)=1.19\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr=\\sqrt{2^2+5^2}=\\sqrt{29}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\sqrt{29},1.95)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/127-p5-2.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\theta=\\arctan(\\tfrac{24}7)=1.29\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr=\\sqrt{7^2+24^2}=\\sqrt{225}=25\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(25,-1.85)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/127-p6-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\theta=\\arctan(\\tfrac{13}{12})=0.825\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nr=\\sqrt{12^2+13^2}=\\sqrt{313}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\sqrt{313},-0.825)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.27-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>Convert each of the following polar coordinates into principal polar coordinates:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(2,\\frac{5\\pi}4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B(1,\\frac{11\\pi}6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C(-1,\\frac\\pi6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D(-2,\\frac{4\\pi}3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Plot each of the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> points in parts a) to d) on a polar coordinate grid.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,-\\frac{3\\pi}4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,-\\frac\\pi6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,-\\frac{5\\pi}6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,\\frac\\pi3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/127-p7-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.27-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>Convert each of the following polar coordinates into Cartesian form:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(3,\\frac\\pi4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B(2,\\frac{5\\pi}6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C(-4,\\frac\\pi3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3\\cos\\frac\\pi4,3\\sin\\frac\\pi4)=(\\frac{3\\sqrt2}2,\\frac{3\\sqrt2}2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2\\cos\\frac{5\\pi}6,2\\sin\\frac{5\\pi}6)=(-\\sqrt3,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-4\\cos\\frac\\pi3,-4\\sin\\frac\\pi3)=(-2,-2\\sqrt3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.27-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>A principal polar coordinate is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,\\frac\\pi3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>Two points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-3,p)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,q)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are known to be the same point as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,\\frac\\pi3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> such that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-3,p)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,q)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;p&lt;2\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\pi&lt;q&lt;4\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-3,\\frac\\pi3+\\pi)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=\\frac{4\\pi}3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,\\frac\\pi3+2\\pi)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q=\\frac{7\\pi}3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.27-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>An equilateral triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has a vertex with polar coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(2,\\frac\\pi6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the possible set of polar coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>the pole <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is at the centre of the triangle.</p></li><li><p>vertex <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is at the pole.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Each vertex is one rotation of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{2\\pi}3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> about the pole</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(2,\\frac\\pi6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B(2,\\frac\\pi6+\\frac{2\\pi}3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C(2,\\frac\\pi6+\\frac{4\\pi}3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>So</p>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(2,\\frac\\pi6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B(2,\\frac{5\\pi}6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C(2,-\\frac\\pi2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac\\pi3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the angle to rotate from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> about the pole</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac\\pi6+\\frac\\pi3=\\frac\\pi2\\text{ or }\\frac\\pi6-\\frac\\pi3=-\\frac\\pi6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(2,\\frac\\pi6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B(0,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C(2,\\frac\\pi2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(2,\\frac\\pi6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B(0,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C(2,-\\frac\\pi6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.27-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>The points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> have polar coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,\\frac\\pi4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,\\frac{3\\pi}4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,\\frac{17\\pi}{12})\" data-display=\"false\"></span> respectively. Find the area of the triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/1.27/solutions/assets/diagrams/127-p8-1.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\begin{gathered}\n\\frac12\\times3\\times4\\times\\sin(\\frac{3\\pi}4-\\frac\\pi4)+\\frac12\\times4\\times4\\times\\sin(\\frac{17\\pi}{12}-\\frac{3\\pi}4)\\\\\n+\\frac12\\times4\\times3\\times\\sin(\\frac{7\\pi}{12}+\\frac\\pi4)\n\\end{gathered}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n=6\\sin\\frac\\pi2+8\\sin\\frac{2\\pi}3+6\\sin\\frac{5\\pi}6\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n=6+4\\sqrt3+3=9+4\\sqrt3=15.9\\text{ units}^2\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.27-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>A curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has polar equation given by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r=4-3\\sin\\theta\\text{ for }-\\pi&lt;\\theta\\le\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Verify that the point given by polar coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,\\frac\\pi2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> lies on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find the point on the curve which is furthest away from the pole <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find the value of the cartesian coordinates of the point which lies on the curve where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=\\frac\\pi4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> giving your answer in exact form.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>RHS: <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4-3\\sin\\frac\\pi2=4-3=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so the point lies on the line.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-1\\le\\sin\\theta\\le1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"r=4-3\\times(-1)=7\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta=\\frac{3\\pi}2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(7,\\tfrac{3\\pi}2)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=4-3\\sin\\frac\\pi4=4-\\frac{3\\sqrt2}2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(4-\\frac{3\\sqrt2}2)\\cos\\frac\\pi4=(4-\\frac{3\\sqrt2}2)\\frac{\\sqrt2}2=2\\sqrt2-\\frac32\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(4-\\frac{3\\sqrt2}2)\\sin\\frac\\pi4=2\\sqrt2-\\frac32\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2\\sqrt2-\\frac32,2\\sqrt2-\\frac32)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.27-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are positive constants, find the conditions under which polar coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-a,b)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(a,-b)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> describe the same point.</p>","steps":["<p>The two angles must be related by:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nb+\\pi=-b+2\\pi k\\text{ for some integer }k\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n2b=2\\pi k-\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\nb=\\pi k-\\tfrac12\\pi\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\Rightarrow b=\\tfrac12(2k-1)\\pi\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>That is, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\" data-display=\"false\"></span> must be some multiple of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2n+1)\\frac\\pi2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"n\\in\\mathbb Z\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<p>Or directly above or below the pole.</p>"]}]